    "text": "Audio credits\n\nExisting music, field recordings and sound-design catalogue assets. No AI-generated music or sound effects are used by this audio bank.\n\n\u201cJuggernaut\u201d by Scott Buckley \u2014 released under CC BY 4.0. A 75-second excerpt from 1:00\u20132:15 of the existing composition, with short entrance/exit fades; encoded at 24kHz/112kbps for the browser. The excerpt repeats in the game. No new composition or stems were created.\n\u201cCar Engine Loop 96kHz, 4s\u201d by qubodup \u2014 CC BY 3.0, selected from the author's alternative licenses. Recorded and looped by the author. Browser copy encoded to Opus with 3dB headroom; playback speed, filtering and gain respond to the racer.\n\u201cFan motor\u201d by Rvgerxini \u2014 CC0 1.0. A recorded mini-fan motor. The publicly supplied high-quality MP3 preview was excerpted from 0:01\u20130:08, level-adjusted and given short edge fades for turbine playback.\n\u201cWinter wind whistling through window.mp3\u201d by audible-edge \u2014 CC0 1.0. Recorded with a Zoom H2. The public high-quality MP3 preview was excerpted from 0:45\u20131:05, level-adjusted and given short edge fades.\nSci-fi Sounds (2020), Impact Sounds (2019), and Interface Sounds (2020) by Kenney \u2014 CC0 1.0. Selected existing Ogg files are copied unchanged; playback gain and rate vary in the game.\n\nThe supplied \u201cNow this is podracing\u201d selection/overtake clip is preserved separately, unchanged. It is not included in the open audio licenses above.\n\nNo creator endorsement is implied. Return to the game."
